`visibleMenu(nodes, role)` filters a menu tree. `role` must be a non-empty string. `nodes` must be an array of objects with a non-empty string `id`, a non-empty `roles` array of non-empty strings, and a `children` array following the same structure. IDs must be unique across the entire tree. Wrong types or missing structures throw `TypeError`; empty values or duplicate IDs throw `RangeError`.

A node is visible when its roles contain the requested role or the wildcard `'*'`. Hidden parents hide their entire subtree. Preserve sibling order. Return a fully independent tree: every returned node, roles array, and children array must be fresh. Empty input returns `[]`, and neither argument may be mutated.

Known-bad source:
